@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance Law s 72 — "תקופת הקצבה", the period of the child allowance. Row IL-08.
-- Source lines 853-856.
--
-- GAPS.md item 6 of row IL-07: row IL-06 answers the allowance on a day, and the capstone asked it
-- about the first day of each month, declining a month in which a child is born or turns 18 after
-- that day. s 72 says which months are paid: from the 1st of the month in which entitlement arose
-- if it arose by the 15th, otherwise from the 1st of the next month; to the last day of the month in
-- which it ceased; only for a child who lived seven days or left the hospital; and for three months
-- after the month in which a child for whom the allowance was paid died.
--
-- WHAT IS ASKED. For one child's entitlement (the day it arose, and how and when it ended), whether
-- the allowance is paid for a given calendar month. Whether a parent is entitled for the child at
-- all, in whose count, and how much, is ss 65-68 (row IL-06).
--
-- THE PERIOD (assumption A2, the lead's choice, assumed, not ruled; reworded in 0.2.0). s 72 carries
-- no amendment tag in the consolidation (line 853), so its own text answers every month from the
-- Law's commencement, which s 402 fixes on 1 October 1995. This row nevertheless answers months from
-- May 2015 only: a scope chosen so that it composes with row IL-06, which answers days from 1 May 2015
-- (its assumption A1). An earlier month is declined by name, and the refusal says that the limit is
-- this row's scope and not the Law's commencement.
--
-- WHERE THE PERIOD IS APPLIED (0.2.0, BACKLOG IL-20, item 08n-GATE). In 0.1.0 only the export
-- declined; the first-month and last-month rules gave a month before May 2015 to any caller. Now one
-- rule computes both months and places each against the period (before May 2015, or which month from
-- it), and every rule that gives a month declines one before May 2015. The export still answers a
-- month from May 2015 for a child whose payment began, or ended, before it.
--
-- "WAS PAID" (0.2.0, item 08n-PAID). (c) reaches only "ילד שבעדו שולמה קצבת ילדים". Whether an
-- allowance was paid is the Institute's record, an input (assumption A4; fork N2 for a child for whom
-- nothing had been paid). The input is now checked against (a) and (b): where it says an allowance was
-- paid, but (b) excludes the child or (a) makes no month payable up to the month of the death, the
-- rules decline the months that turn on it, the three after the month of the death.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 72 — the period of the allowance`

-- src:853 | סעיף 72 – תקופת הקצבה
-- src:854 | (א) נוצרה זכאות לקצבת ילדים עד 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 באותו חודש; נוצרה הזכאות אחרי 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 בחודש שלאחריו; תשלום הקצבה יסתיים ביום האחרון של החודש שבו נפסקה הזכאות.
-- src:855 | (ב) לא תשולם קצבת ילדים אלא בעד ילד שחי שבעה ימים לפחות או שיצא מבית החולים.
-- src:856 | (ג) נפטר ילד שבעדו שולמה קצבת ילדים, ימשיכו בתשלום הקצבה שלושה חודשים מתום החודש שבו נפטר.

-- A calendar month as one count: twelve times the year plus the month less one. Calendar arithmetic,
-- not an answer of s 72, so it takes no period.
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72 — the month count of` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    `the year` TIMES 12 PLUS `the month` MINUS 1

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d MEANS
    `s 72 — the month count of` (DATE_MONTH d) `of` (DATE_YEAR d)

§§ `The period this row answers`

-- s 402, the commencement of the Law, which this row's period is NOT:
-- src:4314 | סעיף 402 – תחילה
-- src:4315 | תחילתו של נוסח משולב זה היא ביום ז׳ בתשרי התשנ״ו (1 באוקטובר 1995).
@ref NII s 72 has no amendment tag (line 853); row IL-06 (assumption A1) answers days from 1 May 2015
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first month this row answers, as a month count` MEANS
    `s 72 — the month count of` 5 `of` 2015

@ref NII s 72 has no amendment tag (line 853) and s 402 (lines 4314-4315) puts the Law's commencement on 1 October 1995; May 2015 is this row's scope (assumption A2), chosen to compose with row IL-06
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)` MEANS
    REFUSE "this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)"

-- A month s 72 names, placed against the period this row answers: before it, or which month of it.
-- Declared here, not in the nouns module, because it is a rule's answer and not a fact the Institute
-- records (the nouns module's membership test).
DECLARE `A month for section 72, placed against the period this row answers` IS ONE OF
    `a month before May 2015`
    `a month from May 2015, numbered` HAS `the month count` IS A NUMBER

-- `the last month paid` is NOTHING while the entitlement has not ended. Where the child died it is the
-- third month after the month of death if (c) runs on the reading asked (fork N2), the month of death
-- if it does not, and the third month after it where the readings differ. The third field says
-- whether that rests on a payment (a) and (b) did not allow (item 08n-PAID); the fourth, where the
-- readings of fork N2 differ, names the month of the death, after which the months are undecided
-- (0.4.0). Every rule that reaches an undecided month declines it.
DECLARE `The first and last months for which section 72 pays the allowance, placed against the period this row answers` HAS
    `the first month paid`  IS A `A month for section 72, placed against the period this row answers`
    `the last month paid`   IS A MAYBE `A month for section 72, placed against the period this row answers`
    `the months after the death rest on a payment that s 72(a) and (b) did not allow` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month of the death, after which fork N2 leaves the months undecided` IS A MAYBE `A month for section 72, placed against the period this row answers`

§§ `The first and last months`

-- (c) for a child whose allowance is recorded as paid although (a) and (b) made no month payable up
-- to the month of its death (item 08n-PAID). The inputs contradict (a) or (b), and (c) does not say
-- whether its three months follow such a payment; the tester leans to fork N2's "no" ("ימשיכו"
-- presupposes a payment under way), the input to "yes".
@ref NII s 72(a)-(c), lines 854-856: "שבעדו שולמה" read against (a) and (b)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment` MEANS
    REFUSE "an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment"

-- Fork N2 (0.4.0): whether (c) reaches a child for whom no allowance had yet been paid. Three
-- readings (nouns, `A reading of section 72(c) for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`): (c) runs only after a payment (this row's reading in versions 0.1.0 to
-- 0.3.0); (c) runs for any child who dies while entitled; the months the two answer differently are
-- declined. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG, BACKLOG IL-53): declined by default, this row's rule
-- being to decline where the text does not decide. The switch is the rule below; the other readings
-- are a one-line change there. They differ only for a child who died with no payment recorded, and
-- only for the three months after the month of the death.
@ref NII s 72(c), line 856; fork N2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 72(c) for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`
`section 72(c) — the reading this row takes for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it` MEANS
    `section 72(c) is declined where the two readings differ`

@ref NII s 72(c), line 856: "נפטר ילד שבעדו שולמה קצבת ילדים, ימשיכו בתשלום הקצבה"; fork N2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid"

-- The one encoding of (a) and (c). Each month is a month count, computed whatever the period, and
-- then placed against the period; nothing before May 2015 leaves this rule as a month.
-- (a), first limb: "עד 15 בחודש" is read as up to and including the 15th (fork N1).
-- (a), last limb, and (c): NOTHING while the entitlement has not ended.
-- (c) reaches a child "for whom a child allowance was paid"; whether it reaches one for whom none had
-- yet been paid is fork N2, read as `r` says.
-- Whether one was paid is an input; it is read against (a) and (b): a payment for a child (b)
-- excludes, or for whom (a)'s first month comes after the month of death, is one s 72 did not allow.
-- On the reading that (c) runs for any child who dies while entitled, the record is not read.
@ref NII s 72(a), (b), (c), lines 854-856; fork N2
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
      r IS A `A reading of section 72(c) for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`
GIVETH A `The first and last months for which section 72 pays the allowance, placed against the period this row answers`
`s 72(a), (c) — the first and last months for which the allowance is paid, placed against the period this row answers, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` r MEANS
    `The first and last months for which section 72 pays the allowance, placed against the period this row answers` WITH
        `the first month paid` IS `placed` `the first month, as a month count`
        `the last month paid`  IS
            CONSIDER `the last month, as a month count`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`placed` n)
        `the months after the death rest on a payment that s 72(a) and (b) did not allow` IS
            CONSIDER e's `how it ended`
            WHEN `the child died on` d THEN     `the payment record is read`
                                            AND e's `a child allowance was paid for the child`
                                            AND `(a) and (b) make no month payable up to the month of` d
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the month of the death, after which fork N2 leaves the months undecided` IS
            CONSIDER e's `how it ended`
            WHEN `the child died on` d THEN
                IF       `the readings of fork N2 are both asked`
                     AND NOT e's `a child allowance was paid for the child`
                THEN JUST (`placed` (`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d))
                ELSE NOTHING
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the day it arose` MEANS e's `the day the entitlement arose`
        `the first month, as a month count` MEANS                                        -- (a), first and second limbs
            IF   DATE_DAY `the day it arose` AT MOST 15
            THEN `s 72 — the month count of the month of` `the day it arose`
            ELSE `s 72 — the month count of the month of` `the day it arose` PLUS 1
        `the last month, as a month count` MEANS
            CONSIDER e's `how it ended`
            WHEN `it has not ended` THEN NOTHING
            WHEN `it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` d THEN JUST (`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d)
            WHEN `the child died on` d THEN
                IF   `(c) runs for this child`
                THEN JUST (`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d PLUS 3)                           -- (c)
                ELSE JUST (`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d)                                  -- (a): entitlement ceased on the death
        `(c) runs for this child` MEANS                                                  -- fork N2; where both are asked, the later month, marked undecided
            CONSIDER r
            WHEN `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child` THEN e's `a child allowance was paid for the child`
            WHEN `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`         THEN TRUE
            WHEN `section 72(c) is declined where the two readings differ`         THEN TRUE
        `the payment record is read` MEANS
            CONSIDER r
            WHEN `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the readings of fork N2 are both asked` MEANS
            CONSIDER r
            WHEN `section 72(c) is declined where the two readings differ` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `(a) and (b) make no month payable up to the month of` d MEANS
                (NOT e's `the child lived at least seven days or left the hospital`)                    -- (b)
            OR  (`the first month, as a month count` GREATER THAN `s 72 — the month count of the month of` d) -- (a): the window is empty
        `placed` n MEANS
            IF   n LESS THAN `the first month this row answers, as a month count`
            THEN `a month before May 2015`
            ELSE `a month from May 2015, numbered` n

-- The rule of versions 0.2.0 to 0.3.0, by its old name, now at the reading the switch names.
@ref NII s 72(a), (b), (c), lines 854-856; the switch above
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A `The first and last months for which section 72 pays the allowance, placed against the period this row answers`
`s 72(a), (c) — the first and last months for which the allowance is paid, placed against the period this row answers, for` e MEANS
    `s 72(a), (c) — the first and last months for which the allowance is paid, placed against the period this row answers, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) — the reading this row takes for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`

-- The first month alone, as a month count; declined if it is before May 2015 (item 08n-GATE). No
-- reading of fork N2 touches it.
@ref NII s 72(a), line 854
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e MEANS
    CONSIDER (`s 72(a), (c) — the first and last months for which the allowance is paid, placed against the period this row answers, for` e)'s `the first month paid`
    WHEN `a month before May 2015`               THEN `this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)`
    WHEN `a month from May 2015, numbered` n     THEN n

-- The last month alone, as a month count; NOTHING while the entitlement has not ended; declined if
-- it is before May 2015 (item 08n-GATE), if it rests on a payment (a) and (b) did not allow (item
-- 08n-PAID), or if the readings of fork N2 put it in different months (0.4.0).
@ref NII s 72(a), (c), lines 854, 856; fork N2
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
      r IS A `A reading of section 72(c) for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the months`'s `the last month paid`
    WHEN NOTHING                                         THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `a month before May 2015`                  THEN `this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)`
    WHEN JUST (`a month from May 2015, numbered` n)      THEN
        IF   `the months`'s `the months after the death rest on a payment that s 72(a) and (b) did not allow`
        THEN `an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment`
        ELSE CONSIDER `the months`'s `the month of the death, after which fork N2 leaves the months undecided`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST n
             OTHERWISE `section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid`
    WHERE
        `the months` MEANS `s 72(a), (c) — the first and last months for which the allowance is paid, placed against the period this row answers, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` r

-- By its old name, at the reading the switch names.
@ref NII s 72(a), (c), lines 854, 856; the switch above
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e MEANS
    `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) — the reading this row takes for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`

§§ `Whether a month is paid`

-- A month from May 2015 is paid if (b) holds, payment has begun by it and has not ended before it.
-- (b) is one input, which the caller answers: how "שבעה ימים" are counted (fork N5) and whether a
-- child born at home and never in a hospital "יצא מבית החולים" (fork N6) are the caller's (0.2.0, item
-- 08n-72B; NOTES.md, fork register).
-- Payment that began before May 2015 has begun by every month this row answers; payment that ended
-- before May 2015 has ended before every one.
-- Item 08n-PAID: where the months after a death rest on a payment (a) and (b) did not allow, a month
-- after the third month is unpaid on either reading of (c), and is answered; a month from the death to
-- the third month after it is declined. A month up to the death never reaches that test: (b) fails, or
-- (a)'s first month is after the death, so the month is unpaid on the text.
-- Fork N2 (0.4.0): where its readings differ, a month after the month of the death and up to the third
-- month after it is declined; the month of the death and those before it are paid or not on (a) and
-- (b) alone, and a month after the third is unpaid on both readings.
@ref NII s 72, lines 853-856; fork N2
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      e           IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
      r           IS A `A reading of section 72(c) for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` r MEANS
    IF   `this month` LESS THAN `the first month this row answers, as a month count`
    THEN `this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)`
    ELSE     e's `the child lived at least seven days or left the hospital`                      -- (b)
         AND `payment has begun by this month`                                                   -- (a), first and second limbs
         AND `payment has not ended before this month`                                           -- (a), last limb, and (c)
    WHERE
        `this month` MEANS `s 72 — the month count of` `the month` `of` `the year`
        `the months` MEANS `s 72(a), (c) — the first and last months for which the allowance is paid, placed against the period this row answers, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` r
        `payment has begun by this month` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the months`'s `the first month paid`
            WHEN `a month before May 2015`               THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a month from May 2015, numbered` first THEN `this month` AT LEAST first
        `payment has not ended before this month` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the months`'s `the last month paid`
            WHEN NOTHING                                         THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST `a month before May 2015`                  THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST (`a month from May 2015, numbered` last)   THEN
                IF        `this month` GREATER THAN last
                THEN      FALSE
                ELSE IF   `the months`'s `the months after the death rest on a payment that s 72(a) and (b) did not allow`
                     THEN `an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment`
                     ELSE CONSIDER `the months`'s `the month of the death, after which fork N2 leaves the months undecided`
                          WHEN NOTHING                                            THEN TRUE
                          WHEN JUST `a month before May 2015`                     THEN `section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid`
                          WHEN JUST (`a month from May 2015, numbered` death)     THEN
                              IF   `this month` GREATER THAN death
                              THEN `section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid`
                              ELSE TRUE

-- The export, by its old name, at the reading the switch names (0.4.0: declined where fork N2's
-- readings differ).
@export Whether the National Insurance Institute pays the child allowance for a child for a given calendar month (from May 2015), under National Insurance Law s 72: from the month entitlement arose (if by the 15th) or the next, to the month it ceased, three months on after a death, and only for a child who lived seven days or left the hospital
@ref NII s 72, lines 853-856; the switch above
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
          @desc the calendar month, 1 to 12
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
          @desc the calendar year
      e           IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
          @desc the day entitlement for the child arose, how and when it ended, whether the child lived seven days or left the hospital, and whether an allowance was paid for the child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, for` e MEANS
    `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, for` e `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) — the reading this row takes for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it`
